 ## Background
-Uniform scaling of SDFs is a fundamental technique in ray marching for implicit surfaces. It was popularized in the context of real-time ray marching shaders, notably by Jamie Wong [S1, unofficial][S3, unofficial]. The method relies on the mathematical property that scaling a space by $s$ and then measuring distance requires multiplying the result by $s$ to maintain the metric properties of the signed distance field. It is widely used in procedural geometry generation and real-time rendering engines.
+The technique applies the inverse transformation to the query point before evaluating the base SDF, then scales the returned distance to compensate for non-rigid distortion [S1, unofficial][S3, unofficial].
 
